From fb37cf265bc70f5942b7e9a54f58b7aa6e83d46d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:01:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(machines): state the DNM 5700 travel as full strokes
 each way

doosan-dnm.mch stated Z in the machine frame (-510..0) and X/Y as half
strokes, so the post gate refused every move above the work origin (the
#457 defect). It now states -1020..1020, -570..570 and -510..510, per the
travel rule in assets/machines/AGENTS.md.

Pinned in vmc_stroke.rs: the DNM bands, a plate contour passing the
stroke check, and a 520 mm clearance still refused by name. The DNM's
optional A has no nose_to_axis, and that separately refuses the post;
it is filed as #1433.

Fixes #1410

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
